  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "The Book of Helaman",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Pahoran the second becomes chief judge and is murdered by Kishkumen—Pacumeni fills the judgment seat—Coriantumr leads the Lamanite armies, takes Zarahemla, and slays Pacumeni—Moronihah defeats the Lamanites and retakes Zarahemla, and Coriantumr is slain. About 52–50 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now behold, it came to pass in the commencement of the fortieth year of the reign of the judges over the people of Nephi, there began to be a serious difficulty among the people of the Nephites.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:1",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For behold, Pahoran had died, and gone the way of all the earth; therefore there began to be a serious contention concerning who should have the judgment-seat among the brethren, who were the sons of Pahoran.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Alma 50:40."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 50:40.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 50:40",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 50,
                    "end": 50,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 40,
                        "end": 40
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:2",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Now these are their names who did contend for the judgment-seat, who did also cause the people to contend: Pahoran, Paanchi, and Pacumeni.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:3",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Now these are not all the sons of Pahoran (for he had many), but these are they who did contend for the judgment-seat; therefore, they did cause three divisions among the people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 151,
            "end": 160,
            "text": "Matt. 12:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Matt. 12:25.",
            "prettyString": "Matthew 12:25",
            "references": [
              {
