        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:12",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And now behold, Pacumeni was appointed, according to the voice of the people, to be a chief judge and a governor over the people, to reign in the stead of his brother Pahoran; and it was according to his right. And all this was done in the fortieth year of the reign of the judges; and it had an end.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "Hel. 1:5; 2:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
