        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:13",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass in the forty and first year of the reign of the judges, that the Lamanites had gathered together an innumerable army of men, and armed them with swords, and with cimeters and with bows, and with arrows, and with head-plates, and with breastplates, and with all manner of shields of every kind.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 149,
            "end": 154,
            "text": "Alma 2:12; 49:6 (6, 24)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "The Book of Helaman 1:14",
        "book": "The Book of Helaman",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And they came down again that they might pitch battle against the Nephites. And they were led by a man whose name was Coriantumr; and he was a descendant of Zarahemla; and he was a dissenter from among the Nephites; and he was a large and a mighty man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 128,
